# Module: doc-drift-gate

Verifies that repo-relative path references in `docs/process/` and the harness
adapters resolve to real files. Runs via `process-gates` (in CI when a CI adapter is installed, and in the pre-push hook) and locally via
`python scripts/process/check_doc_drift.py`.

Installed for **{{ project_name }}**. Rationale: anchors that name files or paths
must stay true as code moves (mandatory rule 1). Only slash-containing references
are checked; bare filenames and placeholders are ignored to avoid false positives.

The gate also watches the **anchor budget**: an anchor file (`CLAUDE.md`,
`AGENTS.md`, or a harness instructions file) over 200 lines (env
`ANCHOR_LINE_BUDGET`) gets a note — never a failure. Anchors regrow silently;
the note flags accretion so a human applies the discriminator from
`docs/process/start-here.md` ("does it drift on a refactor? then it does not
belong in the anchor") and moves detail back to its canonical source.
